From: bradent27-sketch <304192343+bradent27-sketch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 08:21:12 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Retire v2_td_volume_shrink and v2_td_career_regress (rejected
 cold-start WR/TE TD-rate regressions)

Both off since 2026-09-08, backtested and rejected on week 1 2022-2025:
- v2_td_volume_shrink: ALL +0.024*, TE +0.099*, startable WR/TE receiving_tds MAE +0.030* (all CI excludes 0, worse); no
  TD_VOLUME_SHRINK_STRENGTH from 0.10 to 1.0 helped.
- v2_td_career_regress: START-WR +0.034..+0.036* gated and ungated; regressing startable TD rates upward loses on this window.
Removes the branches, td_volume_shrunk_prior / career_regressed_td_prior, their constants, the TD-count columns of the
credibility context, the two sweep scripts and the two helper tests. Default boards identical before and after
(.sweeps/board_identity.py: 2022 w1, 2023 w3, 2024 w1, live 2026 w2). Restore with git revert of this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
